{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjVYge6Vdkb8yAvKehob","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013hhB8jsVH4DC9t1Z7SJDug","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"The line opens under a slur carried over from the line before. The first stretch is quarter rest, low D quarter (below the staff), quarter rest, then a barline. That is bar 15 (rest, D4, rest). The slur continuing from bar 14's Bb4 confirms it. Next comes an E4 quarter and a quarter rest. Then a repeat sign (double bar with dots), \"dol.\" and a sharp F#4 quarter, then a barline. That is bar 16: E4, rest, repeat, \"dolce\" F#4. Next is a dotted half on the F# space, with tremolo strokes under it standing for six repeated 8ths. That is bar 17 (six F#4 8ths). Another identical stroked dotted half on F# is bar 18. Then a stroked dotted half sitting slightly higher, on the G line, is bar 19 (six G4 8ths). The line ends at a barline right after it. Everything matches; the copyist just abbreviates the repeated 8ths as stroked dotted halves.","right":true,"insights":"The repeat sign with \"dol.\" and the F# upbeat fix bar 16 firmly, and bars 15 and 17–19 follow by counting barlines. The tremolo shorthand for repeated 8ths is what needed care, and so did telling F# from G in the last bar, since the notes differ by only a step. A sharper image of the note heads in bars 17–19 would make the F#/G call certain."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5304,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5304},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2103349f-90c1-494b-adaf-dd6c4cf7a360","uuid":"54756511-